<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Juancito</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San Juancito is a mining town in the mountains north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tegucigalpa">Tegucigalpa</a>, Honduras. From 1880 it was the centre of operations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york-and-honduras-rosario-mining-company">New York and Honduras Rosario Mining Company</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines made it for decades one of the most important economic centres of the country. Mining declined in the mid-twentieth century, and the town is now a gateway to La Tigra National Park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-juancito.jpg" alt="San Juancito" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Blindc1rca · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SanJuancito2010.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
